{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"a8e48428fa08d799","name":"card_unit_66th_independent","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_66th_independent","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"66th INDEPENDENT","text":"Deployment: Destroy an enemy unit with two adjacent units.","flavorText":"The 66th Independent Infantry Brigade was a unit of the 47th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army during WWII. At the start of the war the 46th Division was tasked with reinforcing the mainland defenses as part of the Western District Army. However, in October 1943, it was temporarily reassigned to the 16th Army and given orders to move south, except for the 46th Artillery Regiment which remained behind. In late November 1943, the Division's 123rd Regiment landed on Sumba Island in the Lesser Sunda Islands. Subsequently, the 46th Division was reassigned to the 19th Army. In February 1944, the 147th Regiment arrived on the nearby Sumbawa Island. The division set up its headquarters there. Unfortunately, the 145th Regiment was unable to be transported and was redirected from Saipan in June 1944 to Iwo Jima under General Kuribayashi’s command. It met its demise during the intense Battle of Iwo Jima in February to March 1945.","faction":"Japan","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":5,"operationCost":1,"attack":8,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_66th_independent","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_66th_independent_title","SourceString":"66th INDEPENDENT","LocalizedString":"66th INDEPENDENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":8,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":5,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_66th_independent_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Destroy an enemy unit with two adjacent units.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Destroy an enemy unit with two adjacent units."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_66th_independent_history","SourceString":"The 66th Independent Infantry Brigade was a unit of the 47th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army during WWII. At the start of the war the 46th Division was tasked with reinforcing the mainland defenses as part of the Western District Army. However, in October 1943, it was temporarily reassigned to the 16th Army and given orders to move south, except for the 46th Artillery Regiment which remained behind. In late November 1943, the Division's 123rd Regiment landed on Sumba Island in the Lesser Sunda Islands. Subsequently, the 46th Division was reassigned to the 19th Army. In February 1944, the 147th Regiment arrived on the nearby Sumbawa Island. The division set up its headquarters there. Unfortunately, the 145th Regiment was unable to be transported and was redirected from Saipan in June 1944 to Iwo Jima under General Kuribayashi’s command. It met its demise during the intense Battle of Iwo Jima in February to March 1945.","LocalizedString":"The 66th Independent Infantry Brigade was a unit of the 47th Division of the Imperial Japanese Army during WWII. At the start of the war the 46th Division was tasked with reinforcing the mainland defenses as part of the Western District Army. However, in October 1943, it was temporarily reassigned to the 16th Army and given orders to move south, except for the 46th Artillery Regiment which remained behind. In late November 1943, the Division's 123rd Regiment landed on Sumba Island in the Lesser Sunda Islands. Subsequently, the 46th Division was reassigned to the 19th Army. In February 1944, the 147th Regiment arrived on the nearby Sumbawa Island. The division set up its headquarters there. Unfortunately, the 145th Regiment was unable to be transported and was redirected from Saipan in June 1944 to Iwo Jima under General Kuribayashi’s command. It met its demise during the intense Battle of Iwo Jima in February to March 1945."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","selectTargetOnPlayedFr